  "secondary_categories": [],
  "slug": "models-prediction-32d8",
  "summary": "January 2026 preprints and a published diffusion-guidance study couple learned objectives directly into generative molecular design.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is objective coupling, in which a learned predictor or defined target directly steers generation. BADGER adds binding-affinity guidance to diffusion models through classifier and classifier-free guidance for structure-based drug design. EnzyPGM jointly generates enzymes and substrate-binding pockets using residue-atom attention and function priors. ProChoreo aligns sequences with MD-derived conformational ensembles to condition an autoregressive binder generator, and the KAN-based framework pairs PPI-score-guided Monte Carlo sequence generation with a positive-unlabeled classifier. What is new is objective definition beyond scalar affinity: conformational ensembles, surface and hotspot features in Surf2Spot, and pocket-level joint generation. MuCO instead decouples backbone design, side-chain packing, and all-atom optimization across stages, so it is not an instance of this coupling.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-01-31"
}
